## 2. User Stories

- **Account and profile:** As a graduate, I want to register and fill in my profile once, so that I do not repeat my skills and constraints in every query.
- **Conversational matching:** As a user, I want to describe what I am looking for in free text and receive a ranked list of vacancies with an explanation of why each one matched.
- **Contextual refinement:** As a user, I want my follow-up message ("can it be remote?") to be understood in the context of the previous turn.
- **Multiple chats:** As a user, I want several parallel chats for different search directions, in the style of ChatGPT or Gemini.
- **Favorites:** As a user, I want to save vacancies (by myself or via the assistant) into collections and browse them as a list — no separate job catalog.
- **Resume upload:** As a user, I want to upload a PDF resume into my library so that my profile skills are pre-filled and the file stays available to Hira.
- **Profile suggestions:** As a user, I want the system to suggest adding skills and preferences learned from chat, with my explicit confirmation.
- **Skill gap:** As a user, I want to see which skills I am missing for an attractive vacancy.
- **Fresh data:** As a user, I want the corpus to refresh automatically and expired vacancies to be marked.
- **Memory control:** As a user, I want to see, edit, and delete what the system has remembered about me, and to turn cross-chat memory off without losing the current chat.
- **Library:** As a user, I want my own files — a PDF resume and Markdown or plain-text preferences, letters, and scripts — that Hira can read, and I want Hira to create or edit Markdown and text only after I confirm.
- **Call:** As a user, I want to talk to Hira inside the app, like a phone call, without opening a chat.

