## 4. Service and API Design

Five services, synchronous REST between them, one shared PostgreSQL instance:

| Service | Stack | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| `web` | Next.js | UI, SSE consumption; talks only to `core-api` |
| `core-api` | Nest.js | Auth, CRUD, search orchestration, schema ownership, Swagger |
| `retrieval-service` | Express | Hybrid retrieval, fusion, re-ranking, explanation |
| `llm-service` | Express | Provider-agnostic LLM gateway: understand, generate, summarize, extract |
| `ingestion-service` | Express | Connectors, normalization, dedup, skill extraction, embedding, cron |
| `embedding-runtime` | HF TEI | Encoder and cross-encoder over HTTP |

**Key public endpoints (`core-api`):**

- `POST /api/v1/auth/register` · `POST /api/v1/auth/login` · `POST /api/v1/auth/refresh` · `POST /api/v1/auth/logout` · `GET /api/v1/auth/me`
- `GET|POST /api/v1/chats` · `GET|PATCH|DELETE /api/v1/chats/{id}` · `GET /api/v1/chats/{id}/messages`
- **`POST /api/v1/chats/{id}/messages`** — primary endpoint; returns an SSE stream of `user-message` → `intent` → `results` → `token`* → `assistant-message` → `done`.
- `POST /api/v1/search` — direct, chat-free search used for debugging and for the evaluation harness.
- `GET /api/v1/vacancies/{id}` · `/similar` · `/skill-gap`
- `GET|POST|PATCH|DELETE /api/v1/favorites` · `/collections`
- `GET|PUT /api/v1/profile` · `GET|PATCH|DELETE /api/v1/memory`
- `GET /health` · `GET /health/ready`

**Key internal endpoints:**

- `retrieval-service`: `POST /internal/v1/search` (accepts a `SearchIntent` plus an `options` object that selects branches and toggles re-ranking — this is what drives the ablation study), `/similar`, `/skill-gap`
- `llm-service`: `/understand`, `/generate` (streaming), `/summarize-chat`, `/extract-memory`, `/extract-skills`, `/parse-resume`, `/title-chat`
- `ingestion-service`: `/runs`, `/reindex`

All services return a single error shape: `{ errorCode, message, details?, requestId }`.

