## 5. Entity Model (PostgreSQL)

Grouped by domain; full column-level detail in `Wiki/04-data-model.md`.

**Users:** `users`, `refresh_tokens`, `user_profiles` (with `profile_embedding vector(1024)`), `user_profile_skills`, `user_memories` (kind, content, embedding, confidence, provenance, expiry).

**Dialogue:** `chats` (title, rolling summary), `messages` (role, content, `intent jsonb`, `diagnostics jsonb`), `message_vacancies` (rank, score, `explanation jsonb`, `retrieved_by`), `search_logs`.

**Favorites:** `collections`, `favorites` (note, application status).

**Vacancies:** `vacancies` (source, external id, document `language`, normalized salary in BYN, freelance rate and project duration, seniority/format/employment enums, status, `content_hash`, `embedding vector(1024)`, generated `search_vector tsvector` whose text-search configuration is chosen per language), `vacancy_chunks` (per-chunk embeddings), `companies`, `locations`, `vacancy_duplicates`.

**Knowledge graph:** `skills` (canonical name, type, optional taxonomy URI, embedding, corpus IDF), `skill_aliases`, `skill_edges` (typed, weighted, with evidence), `vacancy_skills` (importance, weight, evidence span), `occupations`, `occupation_skills`, `occupation_transitions`.

**Operational:** `ingestion_runs`, `feedback`.

**Indexes:** HNSW (`vector_cosine_ops`, `m = 16`, `ef_construction = 64`) on every embedding column; GIN on `search_vector`; GIN trigram on `title`, `companies.normalized_name`, `skill_aliases.alias`; composite B-tree on filter columns; unique `(source, external_id)` on vacancies.

