## 7. Technical Nuances and Optimization

- **Shared contracts.** All DTOs and domain enums live in `packages/contracts` and are imported by every service including the frontend, eliminating the main failure mode of TypeScript microservices — contract drift.
- **Retrieval-side asymmetry done correctly.** The 2026 solution encoded vacancies with a hand-made weighted template (title repeated four times) but encoded queries as raw text, leaving the two in different regions of the same space. The new pipeline uses the encoder's documented query and passage instructions instead.
- **Chunking.** Long descriptions are chunked and embedded separately, then max-pooled to the vacancy, so that detail deep in a description is no longer lost.
- **Vector indexing.** HNSW replaces the sequential scan of the 2026 solution; pgvector iterative scans keep recall stable under selective filters.
- **Embedding invalidation.** Upserts compare `content_hash` and clear stale embeddings — a defect present in the previous implementation.
- **Non-blocking I/O.** All LLM calls are asynchronous with timeouts, bounded retries with exponential backoff, and a circuit breaker; nothing blocks the event loop.
- **Graceful degradation.** LLM unavailable at understanding time falls back to a heuristic intent; unavailable at generation time returns cards without prose; re-ranker unavailable returns fused order. Only retrieval failure surfaces as a 503.
- **Statistics instead of hard-coded heuristics.** The three hand-written domain keyword dictionaries of the 2026 solution are replaced by corpus-derived skill IDF and co-occurrence-weighted graph edges.
- **Observability.** `X-Request-Id` propagates across every hop; per-branch timings, candidate counts, relaxation steps, and token usage are persisted in `search_logs` and `messages.diagnostics`, and exposed through the API rather than discarded.
- **Cross-lingual retrieval.** BGE-M3 is trained for cross-lingual search, so a Russian query retrieves English vacancies from LinkedIn and Indeed without translating the corpus; the skill graph reinforces this by carrying aliases in both languages on the same node, with ESCO's English labels acting as the pivot.
- **Evaluation as a first-class feature.** The `options` field of the internal search endpoint selects branches and toggles re-ranking, so the entire ablation study runs against the production code path with no code changes. Each benchmark query's `SearchIntent` is computed once and cached on disk, so every ablation configuration receives an identical intent and metric differences are attributable to retrieval alone.
- **Security.** argon2id password hashing, refresh-token hashes at rest with reuse detection, internal services unreachable from outside the Docker network, provider keys only in environment variables, no direct user identifiers sent to external LLM providers.
- **Scraping discipline.** robots.txt is honoured, official APIs are preferred wherever they exist, only public pages are fetched, no authentication or anti-bot circumvention is attempted, and no personal data is collected — only job postings, which are public offers. Connector contract tests run against stored HTML fixtures so the suite needs no network.
